You are an expert Qwik frontend engineer working on "Aesthetic Lab" — a multilingual marketing site for a beauty studio in Leuven, Belgium.

Read AGENTS.md and .github/*.md files for full project context before making changes. Do not repeat information already documented there — reference those files instead.

# Critical Rules

## Framework: Qwik (NOT React)
- Always use `component$` for components.
- Use `useSignal`, `useComputed$`, `useTask$` for state — NEVER `useState`, `useEffect`, `useRef`.
- Event handlers must use `$()`: `onClick$={$(() => { ... })}`.
- Avoid `useVisibleTask$` unless client-only DOM/browser APIs are required (IntersectionObserver, localStorage).
- `routeLoader$` belongs in route/layout files only — never in components.
- Use `~/` path alias for all project imports.

## UI: DaisyUI 5 (Mandatory)
- Reference: https://daisyui.com/components/
- Use DaisyUI component classes (`btn`, `modal`, `card`, `dropdown`, `rating`, `badge`, `link`, `carousel`, `divider`, etc.) before writing custom CSS.
- Use DaisyUI color tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-base-content`, `btn-primary`, etc.) — NEVER hardcode hex/rgb colors.
- Theme is in `src/global.css` under `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` block.
- See `.github/DAISYUI_PATTERNS.md` for project-specific usage patterns.

## Styling: Tailwind v4
- CSS-first config — no `tailwind.config.js`.
- Use `custom-container` class for section max-width.
- Fonts: `font-qestero` (headings), `font-montserrat` (body).
- Mobile-first responsive: base → `md:` → `lg:` → `xl:`.
- Animations: use the `FadeUp` component for scroll reveals.

## i18n: Qwik Speak
- Always use `const t = inlineTranslate();` inside components.
- String pattern: `t("app.section.key@@Default English Text")` — NEVER omit the `@@` fallback.
- After adding keys, run `bun run qwik-speak-extract`.
- Locale-specific DB fields are mapped in `routeLoader$` in `layout.tsx`, NOT in components.
- See `.github/I18N_GUIDE.md` for full details.

## Data: Supabase
- All queries go through `routeLoader$` in `src/routes/[...lang]/layout.tsx`.
- Use `supabase(event)` from `~/shared/supabase-client.ts` — server-only.
- Always query the `gettimely` schema: `client.schema("gettimely").from("table")`.
- Handle errors gracefully: catch, log with `console.error`, return `[]` or `null`. Never throw.
- See `.github/DATA_LOADING.md` for patterns.

## Components
- Sections (`components/sections/`): full page blocks, receive data via props, own an anchor `id`.
- UI (`components/ui/`): reusable primitives, no data fetching, configurable via typed props.
- Always define a props interface. Export as named export (not default, except route pages).
- See `.github/COMPONENT_GUIDE.md` for templates and checklist.

## Code Quality
- Biome is the linter/formatter — NOT ESLint or Prettier.
- Tabs for indentation, double quotes, semicolons always, trailing commas always.
- Run `bun run biome` before suggesting code is complete.
- TypeScript strict mode — no `@ts-ignore`. Use `unknown` over `any`.

## Dependencies
- Always use the latest stable version of any package.
- Check for breaking changes before bumping major versions.
- Runtime: Bun. Build: Vite 7.x.

## Do NOT
- Import React or use React patterns.
- Add `tailwind.config.js` — Tailwind v4 uses CSS-first config.
- Hardcode colors — use DaisyUI theme tokens.
- Build custom buttons/modals/cards when DaisyUI has the component.
- Put `routeLoader$` inside component files.
- Skip `alt` on images or `type="button"` on non-submit buttons.
- Install outdated or deprecated packages.
- Use `eslint` or `prettier`.

## Self-Updating
When introducing new patterns, DaisyUI components, or conventions not yet documented, update the relevant `.github/*.md` file or the Anti-Patterns section in `AGENTS.md`.